# Offline Sync Guidelines

## Scope / Flexibility Notice
These guidelines establish patterns for implementing offline-first capabilities with reliable data synchronization. While specific sync strategies may vary by data type, the core principles remain consistent.

## Best Practices
- Implement local-first data operations with remote sync
- Design conflict resolution strategies for each data type
- Use optimistic UI updates with rollback capability
- Track sync status for all offline-stored entities
- Implement proper queue management for pending operations
- Use logical timestamps or vector clocks for ordering
- Implement delta syncing when possible
- Design efficient batch operations for sync
- Implement proper error recovery for interrupted syncs

## File / Project Structure Guidelines
- Organize sync-related components:
  ```
  lib/
    core/
      sync/
        sync_manager.dart
        sync_worker.dart
        conflict_resolver.dart
    data/
      datasources/
        local/
          sync_queue_store.dart
          entity_changelog.dart
      repositories/
        base_syncing_repository.dart
    domain/
      entities/
        sync_status.dart
        entity_change_record.dart
      usecases/
        trigger_sync_usecase.dart
  ```

## Coding & Styling Conventions
- Use enum for sync states: `SyncStatus.pending`, `SyncStatus.completed`
- Implement metadata for tracking changes: `lastModified`, `syncVersion`
- Implement repository methods like `getLocal`, `getRemote`, `sync`
- Prefix sync-specific events: `EntitySyncStarted`, `EntitySyncCompleted`
- Use consistent change tracking across entities
- Implement proper retry policies for all network operations
- Document sync conflict resolution strategies

## Performance & Optimization Tips
- Implement selective sync for large datasets
- Use batching for sync operations
- Implement efficient diff algorithms
- Use binary formats for local storage
- Compress data for sync operations when appropriate
- Schedule syncs based on data priority and network conditions
- Avoid blocking UI during sync operations
- Implement background sync workers
- Use change tracking to minimize sync payload sizes

## Testing & Validation Guidelines
- Test sync operations under various network conditions
- Simulate conflicts and verify resolution
- Test recovery from interrupted sync operations
- Verify data consistency after sync completion
- Test batch sync operations with large datasets
- Validate offline capability during airplane mode
- Test sync queue persistence across app restarts
- Implement stress testing for sync operations
- Verify memory usage during large sync operations